WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.620
Settle somewhere you can safely give attention to listening.

2
00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:09.510
Your eyes may stay open, softly focused, or closed.

3
00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:16.210
Feel the body supported and notice one point of contact that can help you remain oriented.

4
00:00:23.833 --> 00:00:25.663
Begin with the nearest sound you can hear.

5
00:00:27.363 --> 00:00:31.953
It may come from your breathing, clothing, the room, or something just beyond it.

6
00:00:33.653 --> 00:00:35.163
Let the sound reach you.

7
00:00:36.863 --> 00:00:38.873
There is no need to lean toward it.

8
00:00:50.308 --> 00:00:52.638
Now listen for a more distant sound.

9
00:00:54.338 --> 00:00:56.308
You do not need to identify its source.

10
00:00:58.008 --> 00:01:02.758
Notice its texture, rhythm, volume, or changing edge.

11
00:01:04.458 --> 00:01:07.678
If it disappears, let the disappearance be part of what you hear.

12
00:01:26.736 --> 00:01:29.296
Allow near and far sounds into the same field.

13
00:01:30.996 --> 00:01:34.166
Some may be pleasant, some unwanted, and some neutral.

14
00:01:35.866 --> 00:01:38.556
Listening does not require you to approve of a sound.

15
00:01:40.256 --> 00:01:43.026
It only asks you to recognize that sound is present.

16
00:02:05.895 --> 00:02:11.515
Notice how quickly the mind names what it hears: traffic, voice, machine, bird, music.

17
00:02:13.215 --> 00:02:15.115
Naming is natural.

18
00:02:16.815 --> 00:02:20.005
After the name appears, return to the direct qualities of the sound.

19
00:02:21.705 --> 00:02:22.655
High or low.

20
00:02:24.355 --> 00:02:25.875
Steady or broken.

21
00:02:27.575 --> 00:02:28.965
Close or distant.

22
00:02:51.835 --> 00:02:54.335
Listen for the beginning of a sound.

23
00:02:56.035 --> 00:02:57.845
Then listen for its ending.

24
00:02:59.545 --> 00:03:03.595
Many sounds do not have a clear boundary, so notice whatever change is available.

25
00:03:05.295 --> 00:03:09.625
A sound may fade, be covered by another, or continue beyond your attention.

26
00:03:36.306 --> 00:03:38.676
Include the quiet around sounds.

27
00:03:40.376 --> 00:03:43.126
Quiet does not have to mean complete silence.

28
00:03:44.826 --> 00:03:50.396
It can be the space in which small sounds become clear, or the brief interval before the next sound arrives.

29
00:04:17.077 --> 00:04:21.457
If a sound pulls you into a story or reaction, feel the support beneath the body.

30
00:04:23.157 --> 00:04:27.747
Notice whether the reaction appears as tension, warmth, movement, or thought.

31
00:04:29.447 --> 00:04:33.227
Let that response belong to the field too, without needing to solve it.

32
00:04:56.096 --> 00:04:58.756
Now receive sound from every direction.

33
00:05:00.456 --> 00:05:04.316
In front, behind, to either side, above, or below.

34
00:05:06.016 --> 00:05:08.126
You do not need to map the room accurately.

35
00:05:09.826 --> 00:05:11.906
Let hearing be wide and effortless.

36
00:05:42.399 --> 00:05:44.119
For a while, stop choosing sounds.

37
00:05:45.819 --> 00:05:48.819
Allow hearing to organize itself.

38
00:05:50.519 --> 00:05:53.789
A sound comes forward, changes, and gives way.

39
00:05:55.489 --> 00:05:56.469
Attention may follow.

40
00:05:58.169 --> 00:06:00.929
When you notice thinking, simply listen again.

41
00:06:39.044 --> 00:06:42.524
Bring the sound of breathing into the wider field if it can be heard.

42
00:06:44.224 --> 00:06:47.514
If not, feel the breath while continuing to listen.

43
00:06:49.214 --> 00:06:52.174
Body, breath, and room are happening together.

44
00:07:11.232 --> 00:07:13.842
Choose one sound for a final moment of close listening.

45
00:07:15.542 --> 00:07:17.782
Hear its detail without trying to hold it.

46
00:07:19.482 --> 00:07:22.902
Then release the choice and receive the whole soundscape again.

47
00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:44.230
Let your gaze become clear.

48
00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:51.010
Notice a visible shape and feel the body in its full position.

49
00:07:52.710 --> 00:07:55.270
Sounds will continue after the practice ends.

50
00:07:56.970 --> 00:08:00.000
You can use one of them as a simple invitation to arrive again.
